gh, Paradox will back down on its current course of not approving anything CoD. That\u2019s the best bet at the moment.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, only if/when Paradox finally sells the IP to someone who wants to let Onyx Path to work.<br /> <br /> The current situation is that Paradox thinks that CofD will rob WoD 5 of much needed players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just Curseborne doing well, but far more importantly, WoD5 doing worse.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Bloodlines 2 needs to flop to even have a remote chance of a CofD or Legacy WoD comeback, even then it's iffy because of sunk cost fallacies<br /> <br /> Now, if Bloodlines 2 winds up as a colossal flop on the levels of Conord, Daikatana, or Duke Nukem Forever, then Paradox will be more likely cut their losses and at least sell off/re-license CofD. Bonus points if that happens in conjuction with Curseborne making a profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T07:30:28-07:00","id":1543145,"title":"","content":"There might be no Onyx Path CofD books on the horizon, but some of the company's freelancers took to writing supplements on the Storyteller's Vault. So far, they only published one Changeling book, with no other announced:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/470934/Book-of-Seemings\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Seemings</a><br /> <br /> Maybe that will help take the edge off. 